11 PROCEDURES FOR PREVENTION OF RUNWAY INCURSION OCCURRENCES

11.1 In addition to the procedures set forth in chapters 4, 6, and 10, the following procedures must be observed:

a) whenever issuing a clearance for landing or takeoff, TWR-CT shall perform a visual scan of the runway and, whenever possible, visually monitor aircraft movement while on the runway (takeoff roll, landing, or taxi);

b) clearance for the start of construction works must be issued exclusively via CCR- SBCT Radio;

c) the completion of works and release of the runway for return to operations must be communicated by CCR-SBCT via CCR-SBCT Radio;

d) in the call prior to the start of works, the start and end of services must be coordinated, and when possible, if requested, the estimated time for runway release shall be provided, reaffirming that clearance for the start will be issued via CCR- SBCT Radio;

e) runway lights may only be turned off and the runway made available for works after 15 minutes have elapsed since the last takeoff; and

f) all occurrences must be recorded.

11.2 Information regarding a runway incursion occurrence must, in addition to being recorded, be forwarded by TWR-CT to CCR-SBCT, including the date/time of occurrence, description of the incursion, measures adopted, and observed consequences, to the following email addresses:  supervisores.spe.cwb@grupoccr.com.br  safety.cwb@grupoccr.com.br  _ri.dtceact@fab.mil.br

