Even though there are recommended practices issued by the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) concerning go-arounds, the Investigation believes that except where necessary for safety reasons, ICAO should align the practices and procedures with that of the published missed approach procedures followed by pilots.

The Tower controller who communicated with UAE521 would not have been aware that the B777 would have taken at least 60 seconds for the Aircraft to reach 2,000 ft radio altitude after initiation of a normal go-around close to the runway. When he communicated with the flight crew, the Aircraft was airborne for four seconds and passing 58 ft radio altitude. The Investigation believes that air traffic controllers standards and recommended practices should include guidance on when to safely initiate communication with the flight crew after initiation of a go-around.

