10.2.5 The NSA shall approve such personnel, as it sees fit, to carry out such examinations or assessments as it requires ensuring the applicants for ATSEP licenses are competent and meet the appropriate requirements. The NSA shall clearly define and document the roles and responsibilities of those it approves to conduct examinations or assessments within the licensing process. The documentation shall include details of;

a) the agency on whose behalf the examinations or assessments are conducted

b) any certification process required by the NSA including specialist training or specific ATSEP experience requirements

c) the procedures to ensure that those conducting examinations or assessments are competent to do so.

10.3 Continuation Training

10.3.1 Ratings and qualifications on ATSEPs’ licence shall be kept valid through approved continuation training. Units must have procedures, which include Refresher Training, to ensure that ATSEP remain competent in the provision of safety related services for which their system/equipment ratings are valid. Continuation Training shall consist of refresher courses, emergency training and, where appropriate, linguistic training.

10.3.2 Continuation Training shall be given periodically to all holders of an ATSEP licence. Additional training may be provided at the request of individuals or when considered necessary.

10.3.3 The continuation training shall consist of theoretical and practical instructions, when appropriate and shall include:

a) Review and maintenance of operational and technical standards and correction of adverse general tendencies;

b) Team skills and human factors training;

c) Handling of emergency, unusual or degraded system(s) situations;

d) Lessons Learnt from incident examples;

e) Familiarisation with developments and changes;

ART 11 CERTIFICATION OF TRAINING PROVIDERS

11.1 The provision of training of ATSEPs shall be subject to certification by the NSA.

11.2 Applications for certification may be submitted to the NSA if the applicant has its principal place of operation and, if any, its registered office on the territory of the <country>.

11.3 The requirements for certification shall be detailed by the NSA and shall relate to competence and suitability to organise and provide training (courses) that will fulfil the requirements as set out in Annex C.

Annex C Requirements for Certification of Training Providers

1. Compliance with the requirements referred to in Article 11 shall be demonstrated by evidence that training providers are adequately staffed and equipped and operate in an environment suitable for the provision of the training necessary to obtain or maintain Cadet ATSEP and ATSEP training standards and competences. In particular training providers shall:

(a) have an efficient management structure and sufficient staff with adequate qualifications and experience to provide training according to the standards set out in this Regulation;

(b) have available the necessary facilities, equipment and accommodation appropriate for the type of training offered;

(c) provide the methodology they will use to establish details of the content, organisation and duration of training courses and training plans; this will include the way examinations or assessments will be organised. For examinations related to initial and rating training, including simulation training, the qualifications of the examiners must be indicated in detail;

(d) furnish proof of the quality management system in place to monitor compliance with and the adequacy of the systems and procedures which ensure that the training services provided satisfy the standards set out in this Regulation;

(e) demonstrate that sufficient funding is available to conduct the training according to the standards set out in this Regulation and that the activities have sufficient insurance cover in accordance with the nature of the training provided.

